<title>UK: Braseg Overseas Bk sets two-tranche CD for $65 mln.</title>
<headline>Braseg Overseas Bk sets two-tranche CD for $65 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The following certificate of deposit was announced by lead manager Credit Lyonnais.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BRASEG OVERSEAS BANK</p>
<p> TRANCHE 1</p>
<p> AMT    $40 MLN	 YIELD	7.95 PCT  MATURITY    03.OCT.97</p>
<p> TYPE	 CD	  PAY FREQ   ANNUAL    PAY DATE    09.OCT.96</p>
<p>+ + + +</p>
<p> TRANCHE 2</p>
<p> AMT    $25 MLN	 YIELD	7.50 PCT  MATURITY    09.APR.97</p>
<p> TYPE	 CD	  PAY FREQ   ANNUAL    PAY DATE    09.OCT.96</p>
<p>+ + + +</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS.</p>
<p> DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/FR/UK/BR/CY</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES</p>
<p> NOTES	LAUNCHED ON A DISCOUNT BASIS</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
